{% extends "_base.j2" %}
{% block body %}
You are generating the outline for an IEEE survey paper.

Domain: {{ domain.domain }}
Total word budget: {{ budget.total_words }} (excluding References).

Fixed section plan (ORDER MATTERS):
{% for s in sections %}
- {{ s.name }} (target ≈ {{ s.target_words }} words){% if s.get('members') %} [members: {{ s.get('members') | length }}]{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

Your job:
1. Propose a concise, IEEE-style survey TITLE (≤ 15 words).
2. A 4-sentence ``abstract_brief`` for the abstract stage to expand.
3. 5–8 IEEE-style ``keywords``.
4. For each section above, 3–6 ``bullets`` describing what it should
   cover; bullets should reference corpus keys in square brackets
   (e.g. ``[CITE:<key>]``) where evidence is expected. The actual
   prose will be drafted later; bullets are a skeleton.

Return STRICT JSON (no markdown fence, no commentary):

    {
      "title": "...",
      "abstract_brief": "...",
      "keywords": ["..."],
      "sections": [
        {"name": "<must match one of the fixed names>",
         "bullets": ["...", "..."]}
      ]
    }

Available corpus keys (for CITE references):
{% for item in corpus %}
- {{ item.key }}: {{ item.title }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
